# Swift Concurrency

- Prefer structured concurrency over `Task {}` and `Task.detached` for application code.
- Prefer async/await over callback-based APIs and GCD when modern concurrency is available.
- Treat actor isolation, reentrancy, cancellation, and `Sendable` as correctness concerns.
- Never use `@unchecked Sendable` as a shortcut unless the type is provably synchronized internally.
- Re-check assumptions after every suspension point when working inside actors.
- Wrap legacy completion-handler APIs using checked continuations when bridging to async code.
- Keep concurrency fixes explicit and safe rather than suppressing compiler diagnostics.
